#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0318 expect=violation domain=PC
# Rule:Description: --NOMDY is populated with a value that is not an integer.
#note "Added 2026-09-14 (PLAN-column-type-conformance carried-forward). This rule had NO .cdt scenario at all while its semantics were rewritten from an integer-shaped regex to `not is_integer` — the no-scenario-during-a-rewrite shape. --NOMDY is Num throughout SEND (PC/PP/DS fixtures in this corpus all declare it Num), and on a Num column the retired regex subject now ERRORS under the R9 gate, so this fixture is what distinguishes the migrated rule from the unmigrated one. ⭐ MEASURED 2026-09-14, not argued: restoring `--NOMDY !~ /^-?[0-9]+$/` reds this file and its -valid- twin with the gate's own message. Row 1 is a fractional nominal day and fires; row 2 is whole and must not. ⚠ This covers the FINDINGS leg of Scope.Classes; the EVENTS leg has its own file on DS — the two legs are separate wildcard expansions and a scenario on one proves nothing about the other."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 PCSEQ=1
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCNOMDY type=Num  label="Nominal Study Day for Tabulations"
---
S1 | PC | 001 | 1 | DRUGX | 1.5
S1 | PC | 001 | 2 | DRUGX | 3
---
